From 96a7752ddae03e2bf10d3bff0f7391a418255c87 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Baris Dinc <barisdinc@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 13:59:05 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] library: Add axi_datv_xpdr DATV transponder core

Add a small AXI-Lite controlled core that relays the AD936x RX samples
to the TX path for use as a DATV repeater (transponder). The RF
frequency translation is done by the independent RX/TX LOs of the
AD936x, the core only processes the baseband samples:

- enable/bypass: when disabled the TX path is fed by the regular
  DMA/interpolator data, so normal libiio TX keeps working
- digital gain (unsigned Q4.12) with saturation and a saturation counter
- averaged I^2+Q^2 power detector (IIR, time constant 2^n samples)
- squelch with configurable threshold and hang time, force mute

Control registers cross into the data clock domain with up_xfer_cntrl,
status registers with up_xfer_status.
